log}⁡(x)={log}_{10}⁡(x)$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571385 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "303e2b76-22b6-55f6-abfa-1986d9ab5f9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571385 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))}^{′}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡(x))(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))+(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1069 "q-319824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0fee3ca-7f95-5f0e-a414-4282e409bf7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571432 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=2x+1$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)+1}{1}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104300" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1071 "Differentiate ${x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8004d91-2319-5283-80d1-a0670d83fdc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571442 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({x}^{3})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+({x}^{3})(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1069 "q-320824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f475b19b-1e35-517e-8f15-4fa3d740b6ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571450 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}+3$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2}+3)}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+({x}^{2}+3){(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))+({x}^{2}+3)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
